    <description>ELV-CPQ-119 / TNCI-108: On creation of a renewal Quote, maps the contract cap fields (Renewal Price Cap %, Volume Cap, Discount Cap) forward from the source quote, traversing the renewal Opportunity&apos;s Previous Opportunity link to that Opportunity&apos;s Primary Quote. Caps are stamped once, at insert.
v2: Simplified mapping and insert logic to reduce the amount of GET calls during execution
v3: Added population of quote field Current Renewal Price Cap %

v6: ELV-CPQ-168 / TNCI-222: The system shall set the quote expiration date based on the quote type, defaulting new-business quotes to the end of the following quarter and renewal quotes to a date no earlier than three months before the subscription end date.

v9: Populate quote team
v12: Set default Payment Term from account (via formula to account for unique global picklist requirements - see element for detail)</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Sets Quote.Status to Approved whenever ELV_ApprovalStatus__c is Approved; otherwise passes through the record&apos;s current Status unchanged.</description>
        <name>ApprovedStatusFormula</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(TEXT({!$Record.ELV_ApprovalStatus__c}) = &quot;&quot;, &quot;Draft&quot;, TEXT({!$Record.ELV_ApprovalStatus__c}))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Necessary because Ruby__PaymentTerm__c picklist customization requires special API value handling (https://docs.nue.io/create-custom-payment-terms). Options from account picklist include text values that must be handled by this formula.</description>
        <name>defaultPaymentTermFormulaVar</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>CASE(
    TEXT({!Get_Opportunity.Account.Payment_Terms__c}),
    &quot;Cash with Order (CWO)&quot;, &quot;0&quot;,
    &quot;Not Applicable&quot;, &quot;0&quot;,
    &quot;None - Reseller only&quot;, &quot;0&quot;,
    &quot;Net 15&quot;, &quot;Net 15&quot;,
    &quot;Net 30&quot;, &quot;Net 30&quot;,
    &quot;Net 45&quot;, &quot;Net 45&quot;,
    &quot;Net 60&quot;, &quot;Net 60&quot;,
    SUBSTITUTE(
        TEXT({!Get_Opportunity.Account.Payment_Terms__c}),
        &quot;Net &quot;,
        &quot;&quot;
    )
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>ELV-CPQ-168 Ravus Refined Requirement: The system shall set the quote expiration date based on the quote type, defaulting new-business quotes to the end of the following quarter and renewal quotes to a date no earlier than three months before the subscription end date.

Note: This formula built based on fiscal year start date of Feb 1</description>
        <name>newCustomerQuoteExpirationDateVar</name>
        <dataType>Date</dataType>
        <expression>ADDMONTHS(
    DATE(
        YEAR(TODAY()),
        MONTH(TODAY()),
        1
    ),
    6 - MOD(MONTH(TODAY()) - 2 + 12, 3)
) - 1</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>newQuoteTest</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>ISNEW()</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>ELV-CPQ-168 Ravus Refined Requirement: The system shall set the quote expiration date based on the quote type, defaulting new-business quotes to the end of the following quarter and renewal quotes to a date no earlier than three months before the subscription end date.</description>
        <name>renewalQuoteExpirationDateVar</name>
        <dataType>Date</dataType>
        <expression>{!$Record.Ruby__SubscriptionEndDate__c} - 90</expression>
    </formulas>
